RCDog-SuperMimic is a downstream adaptation of Uni-SuperMimic to the RCDog
12-DoF quadruped. The upstream Uni-SuperMimic framework, G1 task and training
code are licensed under Apache-2.0; the original notice and license text are
preserved in LICENSES/Apache-2.0-Uni-SuperMimic.txt.

The upstream implementation was developed with reference to the SuperMimic
reference code in supermimic_vibed, whose MIT license and copyright notice are
preserved in LICENSES/MIT-supermimic.txt.

SuperMimic paper:
"SuperMimic: Scaling Humanoid Whole-Body Control with One Differentiable
World Model", Qiayuan Liao et al., https://supermimic.github.io

RCDog adaptation, 2026-10-27. The combined software release is distributed
under GPL-3.0-only (root LICENSE). Original Uni-SuperMimic portions retain
their Apache-2.0 notices.

The RCDog robot description, meshes and MJCF under source/ and
src/unisupermimic/assets/robots/rcdog/ are provided by the project author and
are not relicensed by the software GPL. The reference motions under
src/unisupermimic/assets/motions/rcdog/ are generated by
tools/rcdog/generate_omni.py; no third-party motion-capture dataset is
redistributed. Trained weights under results/ and initial_policy/ were produced
by this project and are included so the reported results can be reproduced.

See THIRD_PARTY.md for sources, modifications and scope.

